    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297-a2">

                <pb facs="0591" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in inclosure in No.
                    558.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir H. T. Holland to foreign office.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Downing Street</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 27,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the letter from this
                    office of 10th of July last and to previous correspondence respecting the
                    application of the United States Government for permission to establish stations
                    in Tasmania and New Zealand for the observation of the transit of Venus, I am
                    directed by the Earl of Kimberley to transmit to you, for the information of
                    Earl Granville, a copy of a dispatch from the governor of New Zealand, stating
                    that the instruments required for the observation will be admitted free of
                    duty.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>H. T. HOLLAND.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
